## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces a new DP angle: exact k segments, per-segment cost, and sum-based values, requiring both interval DP and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sums
- DP over i (prefix length) and t (blocks)
- Reconstructing endpoints from choice pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumPartition(A,k,c){
  const n=A.length;
  const P=[0];
  for(const x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1]+x);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const pos=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1]=(P[i]-P[0])-c, pos[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let s=t-1;s<=i-1;s++){
        const val=dp[s][t-1]+(P[i]-P[s])-c;
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; pos[i][t]=s; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let i=n, t=k;
  const blocks=[];
  while(t>0){
    const s=pos[i][t];
    blocks.push([s, i-1]);
    i=s; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {score: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests dynamic programming with multiple constraints: non-adjacent blocks, exact block count, and reconstruction requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Disjoint blocks with at least one-element gap between consecutive blocks
- dp[i][t] transitions for skipping elements vs. ending a block
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sum queries
- Backpointers for reconstructing the chosen subarray endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const prefix = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) prefix[i] = prefix[i - 1] + A[i - 1];

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      // Skip element i
      if (dp[i - 1][t] >= dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
        prev[i][t] = { skipped: true };
      }
      // End a block at i
      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const prevIdx = s >= 2 ? s - 2 : 0;
        const val = dp[prevIdx][t - 1] + (prefix[i] - prefix[s - 1]) - c;
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = { skipped: false, start: s };
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruction
  const result = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    const state = prev[i][t];
    if (state.skipped) {
      i--;
    } else {
      result.push({ start: state.start, end: i });
      i = state.start - 2;
      t--;
    }
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks: result.reverse() };
}
```

